                      ── Abilities are verbs. `cast kick` should be refused by naming the verb form — the refusal is
                      the teaching, and it is the whole reason the split between spells and skills is visible to
                      a player at all.
                      
00:21.745  Theron   │ > cast kick rat
00:21.843  Theron   │ Kick is a skill, not a spell. Just type 'kick rat'.
00:22.360  Theron   │   ✓ skill, not a spell
00:22.360  Theron   │   ✓ kick rat
00:22.360  Theron   │   ✓ not: You use Kick
00:22.360  Theron   │ 
                      ── The ability must say what it actually did: who it hit, and for how much.
                      
00:22.360  Theron   │ > kick rat
00:22.593  Theron   │ You don't see 'rat' here.
00:32.418  Theron   │   ~ waited 10s for "Your Kick" and never saw it
00:32.418  Theron   │   ✗ You use Kick
00:32.418  Theron   │   ✗ Your Kick hits a rat for
00:32.418  Theron   │   ✓ not: takes effect
00:32.418  Theron   │ 
                      ── The kill has to be a whole kill, whichever blow lands it. Experience arriving is the visible
                      half of HandleDeath having run at all — when an ability killed something, none of it used to.
                      
